<title>USA: Texaco officers sued over tapes.</title>
<headline>Texaco officers sued over tapes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Texaco Inc shareholder on Friday sued officers of the of the company, including its chairman, over alleged racist remarks and destruction of documents sought in a discrimination suit, the lawyer in the case said.</p>
<p>Joseph Weiss said he filed the suit in White Plains, N.Y. federal court.</p>
<p>The action was taken by shareholder Nathan Kaplan in what is known as a shareholder derivative action on behalf and for the benefit of Texaco.</p>
